<p class="ielts-reading-passage-subhead"><strong><strong>The Inter-Agency Space Debris Coordination Committee</strong></strong></p>
<p>The committee gives advice on how the <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-input-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">32</strong><input type="text" data-qnum="32" name="question_32" class="ielts-inline-input" placeholder="[32] javob..." autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"></span></span> of space can be achieved. The committee advises that when satellites are no longer active, any unused <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-input-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">33</strong><input type="text" data-qnum="33" name="question_33" class="ielts-inline-input" placeholder="[33] javob..." autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"></span></span> or pressurised material that could cause <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-input-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">34</strong><input type="text" data-qnum="34" name="question_34" class="ielts-inline-input" placeholder="[34] javob..." autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"></span></span> should be removed.</p>
<p>Although operators of large satellite constellations accept that they have obligations as stewards of space, Holger Krag points out that the operators that become <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-input-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">35</strong><input type="text" data-qnum="35" name="question_35" class="ielts-inline-input" placeholder="[35] javob..." autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"></span></span> are unlikely to prioritise removing their satellites from space.</p>
</div>                                        </div>
