arrow investigation">J. narrow investigation</option></select></span></span> of 52 hours in a hot-air balloon, followed by his well-publicised but <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-select-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">35</strong><select data-qnum="35" name="question_35" class="ielts-inline-select"><option value="">[ 35 ] Tanlang...</option><option value="A. modest fame">A. modest fame</option><option value="B. vast range">B. vast range</option><option value="C. record-breaking achievement">C. record-breaking achievement</option><option value="D. research methods">D. research methods</option><option value="E. select group">E. select group</option><option value="F. professional interests">F. professional interests</option><option value="G. scientific debate">G. scientific debate</option><option value="H. hazardous exploration">H. hazardous exploration</option><option value="I. biographer’s perspective">I. biographer’s perspective</option><option value="J. narrow investigation">J. narrow investigation</option></select></span></span> of Greenland’s coast. With the publication of his textbook on thermodynamics, he had also come to the attention of a <span class="ielts-reading-question-item"><span class="ielts-inline-select-wrap"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">36</strong><select data-qnum="36" name="question_36" class="ielts-inline-select"><option value="">[ 36 ] Tanlang...</option><option value="A. modest fame">A. modest fame</option><option value="B. vast range">B. vast range</option><option value="C. record-breaking achievement">C. record-breaking achievement</option><option value="D. research methods">D. research methods</option><option value="E. select group">E. select group</option><option value="F. professional interests">F. professional interests</option><option value="G. scientific debate">G. scientific debate</option><option value="H. hazardous exploration">H. hazardous exploration</option><option value="I. biographer’s per